homelab-haproxy (0.1.15) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Every generated server line carries `check inter 10s fastinter 2s
    downinter 5s` (haproxy's own inter is 2s); a backend may set its own
    `check_inter:` in backends.yml, and the example gives imap/imaps 5s. Each
    health check is a logged connection on the backend, and at 2s from three
    proxies the postfix pool wrote 1.4 million probe lines a day and filled a
    root disk (post-cutover #105). Detection of a dead server goes from about
    6s to about 14s at the default; IMAP keeps it under 10s.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0600

homelab-haproxy (0.1.14) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Every TCP frontend binds one dual-stack socket, [::]:port v4v6, so the
    mail and IMAP ports take IPv6 clients too (post-cutover #73); the PROXY
    header carries TCP4 or TCP6 as the client came, the backends stay IPv4.
    The metrics frontend stays *:8404.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:00:00 -0600

homelab-haproxy (0.1.13) unstable; urgency=medium

  * backends.example.yml: the smtps frontend (465 -> the Postfix pool's
    smtps service, send-proxy), post-cutover #70. A fresh install fronts
    465 from the start; an existing site file is never edited by the
    package -- install-orchestrators/smtps-orchestrate.sh adds the entry.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:25:00 -0600

